{"questions":[{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d14860784d","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d14860784d","q":"<p><strong>Evaluate:</strong></p>\n<p>`int1/(x^2 + 25)dx`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let I = `int1/(x^2 + 25)dx`</p>\n<p>= `1/(x^2 + (5)^2)dx`</p>\n<p>= `1/5 tan^-1  x/5 + c`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperDate":"2024-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607821","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607821","q":"<p>Write `int cotx  dx`.</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>`int cotx . dx`</p>\n<p>= `int cosx/sinx . dx`</p>\n<p>`d/dx sin x` = cos x</p>\n<p>= `int ((d/dx sin x)/sin x . dx)`</p>\n<p>= log (sin x) + c</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperDate":"2023-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077f5","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077f5","q":"<p>If f'(x) = x<sup>–1</sup>, then find f(x)</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Given, f'(x) = `1/x`</p>\n<p>On integrating both sides, we get</p>\n<p>f(x) = logx + C</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperDate":"2022-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077cb","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077cb","q":"<p>`int \"dx\"/(9\"x\"^2 + 1)= ______. `</p>","options":["<p>`1/3 \"tan\"^-1(2\"x\") +\"c\"`</p>","<p>`1/3 \"tan\"^-1\"x\" +\"c\"`</p>","<p>`1/3 \"tan\"^-1(3\"x\") +\"c\"`</p>","<p>`1/3 \"tan\"^-1(6\"x\") +\"c\"`</p>"],"answer":2,"solution":"<p>`1/3 \"tan\"^-1(3\"x\") +\"c\"`</p>\n<p>Let I = `int \"dx\"/(9\"x\"^2 + 1)`</p>\n<p>= `1/9 int \"dx\"/((\"x\"^2) +(1/3)^2)`</p>\n<p>= `1/9 1/(1/3) \"tan\"^-1(\"x\"/(1/3)) + \"C\"`</p>\n<p>`= 1/3 \"tan\"^-1(3\"x\") + \"c\"`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"singleCorrect","source":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperDate":"2019-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607875","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607875","q":"<p>The value of `intx^x (1 + logx)dx` is equal to ______.</p>","options":["<p>`1/2(1 + logx)^2 + c`</p>","<p>`x^(2x) + c`</p>","<p>`x^x.logx + c`</p>","<p>`x^x + c`</p>"],"answer":3,"solution":"<p>The value of `intx^x (1 + logx)dx` is equal to `bbunderline(x^x + c)`.</p>\n<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>\n<p>`I = intx^x (1 + logx)dx`</p>\n<p>We recognize that x<sup>x</sup> can be rewritten using the exponential function:</p>\n<p>x<sup>x</sup> = e<sup>xlogx</sup></p>\n<p>Taking the derivative,</p>\n<p>`d/(dx)(x^x) = x^x (1 + logx)`</p>\n<p>Thus, the given integral simplifies directly to:</p>\n<p>`I = int d(x^x) = x^x + c`</p>\n<p>= `x^x + c`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"singleCorrect","source":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperDate":"2025-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607882","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607882","q":"<p><strong>Integrate the following function w.r.t. x:</strong></p>\n<p>x<sup>9</sup>.sec<sup>2</sup>(x<sup>10</sup>)</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let I = `int x^9 .sec^2(x^10).dx`</p>\n<p>Put x<sup>10</sup> = t<br/>∴ 10x<sup>9</sup>dx = dt</p>\n<p>∴ x<sup>9</sup>dx = `(1)/(10)dt`</p>\n<p>∴ I = `int sec^2t.dt/(10)`</p>\n<p>= `1/10 int sec^2t  dt`</p>\n<p>= `(1)/(10)tan t+ c`</p>\n<p>= `(1)/(10)tan(x^10) + c`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperDate":"2025-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607883","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607883","q":"<p><strong>Evaluate the following:</strong></p>\n<p>`int (1)/(25 - 9x^2)*dx`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>I = `int (1)/(25 - 9x^2)*dx`</p>\n<p>= `int(1)/(5^2 - (3x)^2)*dx`</p>\n<p>= `(1)/(2(5))log |(5 + 3x)/(5 - 3x)|*(1)/(3) + c`</p>\n<p>= `(1)/(30)log |(5 + 3x)/(5 - 3x)| + c`</p>\n<p><strong>Alternative Method:</strong></p>\n<p>`int (1)/(25 - 9x^2)*dx`</p>\n<p>= `(1)/(9) int (1)/((25)/(9)x^2)*dx`</p>\n<p>= `(1)/(9) int (1)/((5/3)^2 - x^2)*dx`</p>\n<p>= `(1)/(9) xx (1)/(2 xx 5/3)log|(5/3 + x)/(5 / 3 - x)|+ c`</p>\n<p>= `(1)/(30)log|(5 + 3x)/(5 - 3x)| + c`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperDate":"2025-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607856","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607856","q":"<p><strong>Evaluate:</strong></p>\n<p>`int log x dx`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let `I = int log x dx`</p>\n<p>= `int log x * 1 dx`</p>\n<p>`I = log x int 1 dx - int [int 1 dx * d/dx (log x)] dx`</p>\n<p>= `(log x) (x) - int [x * 1/x] dx`</p>\n<p>= `x log x - int 1 dx`</p>\n<p>∴ I = x log x − x + c</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperDate":"2024-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d14860781c","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d14860781c","q":"<p>`int cos^3x  dx` = ______.</p>","options":["<p>`1/12 sin 3x + 3/4 sin  x + c`</p>","<p>`1/12 sin 3x + 1/4 sin x + c`</p>","<p>`1/12 sin 3x - 3/4 sin x + c`</p>","<p>`1/12 sin 3x - 1/4 sin x + c`</p>"],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>`int cos^3x  dx` = `underlinebb(1/12 sin  3x + 3/4 sin  x + c)`.</p>\n<p><strong>Explanation:</strong></p>\n<p>`int cos^3x . dx`</p>\n<p>cos 3A = 4 cos<sup>3</sup> A – 3 cos A</p>\n<p>I = `int 1/4 (cos 3x + 3 cos x) . dx`</p>\n<p>= `1/4 (sin 3x . 1/3 + 3 . sin x) + c`</p>\n<p>= `1/12 sin 3x + 3/4 sin x + c`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"singleCorrect","source":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperDate":"2023-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077f1","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077f1","q":"<p>If `int (dx)/(4x^2 - 1)` = A log `((2x - 1)/(2x + 1))` + c, then A = ______.</p>","options":["<p>1</p>","<p>`1/2`</p>","<p>`1/3`</p>","<p>`1/4`</p>"],"answer":1,"solution":"<p>If `int (dx)/(4x^2 - 1)` = A log `((2x - 1)/(2x + 1))` + c, then A = `\\underlinebb(1/2)`.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"singleCorrect","source":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperDate":"2022-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077d4","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077d4","q":"<p>Evaluate : `int (\"e\"^\"x\" (1 + \"x\"))/(\"cos\"^2(\"x\"\"e\"^\"x\"))\"dx\"`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let I = `int (\"e\"^\"x\" (1 + \"x\"))/(\"cos\"^2(\"x\"\"e\"^\"x\"))\"dx\"`<br/>Put `\"x\".\"e\"^\"x\" = \"t\"`<br/>Differentiate w.r.t. x,<br/>`\"x\" .\"e\"^\"x\" +\"e\"^\"x\" . 1 = \"dt\"/\"dx\" =&gt; \"e\"^\"x\" (\"x\" +1)\"dx\" =\"dt\"`<br/>`therefore int 1/(\"cos\"^2 \"t\") \"dt\"`</p>\n<p>= ∫ sec<sup>2</sup> t dt<br/>= tan t + c</p>\n<p>` therefore int (\"e\"^\"x\" (1 + \"x\"))/(\"cos\"^2(\"x\"\"e\"^\"x\"))\"dx\" = \"tan\"(\"x\" .\"e\"^\"x\") + \"c\"`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperDate":"2019-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077b6","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077b6","q":"<p>Evaluate `int e^x [(cosx - sin x)/sin^2 x]dx`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>`I = inte^x [cosx/sin^2x - sinx/sin^2x]dx`</p>\n<p>`= int e^x[(cotx.cosecx, -cosecx),(f'(x), f(x))]`</p>\n<p>∵ `int e^x[f(x) + f'(x)]dx  = e^x f(x) + C`</p>\n<p>`:. I = -e^x.cosec x + C`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperDate":"2018-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d148607790","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d148607790","q":"<p>Evaluate: `intsinsqrtx/sqrtxdx`</p>\n<p> </p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>`Let I=int(sinsqrtx/sqrtx)dx`</p>\n<p>`Let sqrtx=t`</p>\n<p>`1/(sqrtx)=dt/dx`</p>\n<p>`1/sqrtxdx=2dt`</p>\n<p>`therefore I=2intsintdt`</p>\n<p>`=-2cost+C`</p>\n<p>`=-2cos(sqrtx)+C`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperDate":"2017-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607863","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607863","q":"<p><strong>Prove that:</strong></p>\n<p>`int 1/(a^2 - x^2) dx = 1/2 a log ((a +x)/(a-x)) + c`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let I = `int1/(a^2 - x^2)dx`</p>\n<p>= `intdx/((a - x)(a + x))`</p>\n<p>= `1/(2a) int (1/(a + x) + 1/(a - x))dx`</p>\n<p>= `1/(2a) [int dx/(a + x) + int dx/(a - x)]`</p>\n<p>= `1/(2a) [log (a + x) + (log (a - x))/-1] + c`</p>\n<p>= `1/(2a) [log (a + x) - log (a - x)] + c`</p>\n<p>= `1/(2a) log ((a + x)/(a - x)) + c`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperDate":"2024-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607837","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607837","q":"<p>Evaluate the following : `int x tan^-1 x .dx`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let I = `int x tan^-1 x .dx`</p>\n<p>= `int (tan^-1 x)x.dx`</p>\n<p>= `(tan^-1 x) int x.dx - int[{d/dx(tan^-1 x) intx.dx}].dx`</p>\n<p>= `(tan^-1x) (x^2/2) - int (1/(1 + x^2)) (x^2/2).dx`</p>\n<p>= `(x^2 tan^-1)/(2) - (1)/(2) int x^2/(x^2 + 1).dx`</p>\n<p>= `x^2/(2) tan^-1x - (1)/(2) ((x^2 + 1)-1)/(x^2 + 1).dx`</p>\n<p>= `x^2/(2)tan^-1x - (1)/(2)[int(1 - 1/(x^2 + 1)).dx]`</p>\n<p>= `x^2/(2)tan^-1x - (1)/(2)[int 1.dx - int(1)/(x^2 + 1).dx]`</p>\n<p>= `x^2/(2)tan^-1 x - (1)/(2)(x - tan^-1x) + c`.</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperDate":"2023-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d14860780a","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d14860780a","q":"<p>Evaluate: `int (dx)/(2 + cos x - sin x)`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let I = `int (dx)/(2 + cos x - sin x)`</p>\n<p>Put `tan  x/2` = t</p>\n<p>⇒ x = 2 tan<sup>–1</sup>t</p>\n<p>∴ dx = `(2 dt)/(1 + t^2)`</p>\n<p>And sin x = `(2t)/(1 + t^2)`, cos x = `(1 - t^2)/(1 + t^2)`</p>\n<p>∴ I = `int 1/(2 + ((1  -  t^2)/(1  +  t^2)) - ((2t)/(1 + t^2))) * (2dt)/(1  +  t^2)`</p>\n<p>= `int (1 + t^2)/(2 + 2t^2 + 1 - t^2 - 2t) * (2dt)/(1 + t^2)`</p>\n<p>= `2int 1/(t^2 - 2t + 3) dt`</p>\n<p>= `2int 1/((t - 1)^2 + (sqrt(2))^2)  dt`</p>\n<p>= `2 xx 1/sqrt(2)  tan^-1  ((t - 1)/sqrt(2)) + C`</p>\n<p>= `sqrt(2)tan^-1 ((tan(x/2) - 1)/sqrt(2)) + C`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperDate":"2022-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077bb","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077bb","q":"<p>Evaluate `int 1/(3+ 2 sinx + cosx) dx`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let I = `int 1/(3+2sinx + cosx) dx`</p>\n<p>Put tan `x/2 = t` Then `dx = 2/(1+ t^2) dt`</p>\n<p>`sinx = (2t)/(1+t^2) and cos x = (1- t^2)/(1+ t^2)`</p>\n<p>`:. I = int  (2dt\"/\" (1+t^2))/(3+2 ((2t)/(1+t^2))+((1-t^2)/(1+t^2)))`</p>\n<p>`= 2int (dt\"/\"(1+t^2))/((3(1+t^2) + 4t + (1-t^2))/(1+t^2))`</p>\n<p>= `2int (dt)/(2t^2 + 4t + 4) = int (dt)/((t+1)^2 + 1)`</p>\n<p>`= tan^(-1) (t + 1) + c`</p>\n<p>`= tan^(-1)[tan (x/2) + 1)] + c`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperDate":"2018-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d148607794","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d148607794","q":"<p>If u and v are two functions of x then prove that</p>\n<p>`intuvdx=uintvdx-int[du/dxintvdx]dx`</p>\n<p>Hence evaluate, `int xe^xdx`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let ` int vdx=w.....(1)`</p>\n<p>`then \" \" (dw)/dx=v.....(2)`</p>\n<p>`Now d/dx(u,w)=u.d/dx(w)+wd/dx(u)`</p>\n<p>`=u.v+w(du)/dx.......\"from\"(2)`</p>\n<p>By definition of integration.</p>\n<p>`u.w=int[u.v+w(du)/dx]dx`</p>\n<p>`=intu.vdx+intw.(du)/dx dx`</p>\n<p>`int u.v dx=u.w-int w (du)/dx dx`</p>\n<p>`=u int v dx-int [(du)/dxintv.dx]dx`</p>\n<p>[next section only required for question 2]</p>\n<p>Hence, `int xe^xdx = x.inte^xdx-int[d/dx x.inte^xdx]dx`</p>\n<p>`=xe^x-int1xxe^xdx`</p>\n<p>`=xe^x-e^x+c`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperDate":"2017-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607898","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607898","q":"<p>Integrate the following functions w.r.t. x : `e^(sin^-1x)*[(x + sqrt(1 - x^2))/sqrt(1 - x^2)]`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let I = `int e^(sin^-1x)[(x + sqrt(1 - x^2))/sqrt(1 - x^2)]*dx`</p>\n<p>= `int e^(sin^-1x) [x + sqrt(1 - x^2)]*(1)/sqrt(1 - x^2)*dx`</p>\n<p>Put sin<sup>–1</sup> x = t</p>\n<p>∴ `(1)/sqrt(1 - x^2) * dx` = dt</p>\n<p>and x = sin t</p>\n<p>∴ I = `int e^t [sin t + sqrt(1 - sin^2 t)]*dt`</p>\n<p>= `int e^t [sin t + sqrt(cos^2t)]*dt`</p>\n<p>= `int e^t(sin t + cos t)*dt`</p>\n<p>Let f(t) = sin t<br/>∴ f'(t) = cos t</p>\n<p>∴ I = `int e^t[f(t) + f'(t)]*dt`</p>\n<p>= e<sup>t</sup> . f(t) + c<br/>= e<sup>t</sup> . sin t + c<br/>= `e^(sin^(–1)x) * x + c`</p>\n<p>= `x * e^(sin^(-1)x) + c`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2025","paperDate":"2025-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d14860786d","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d14860786d","q":"<p><strong>Evaluate:</strong></p>\n<p>`int (5e^x)/((e^x + 1)(e^(2x) + 9)) dx`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let I = `int (5e^x)/((e^x + 1)(e^(2x) + 9)) dx`</p>\n<p>Put e<sup>x</sup> = t</p>\n<p>⇒ e<sup>x</sup>dx = dt</p>\n<p>∴ I = `int  5/((t + 1)(t^2 + 9))dt`</p>\n<p>Let `5/((t + 1)(t^2 + 9))`</p>\n<p>= `A/(t + 1) + (Bt + C)/(t^2 + 9)`</p>\n<p>∴ 5 = A(t<sup>2</sup> + 9) + (Bt + C)(t + 1)    ...(i)</p>\n<p>Putting t = –1 in (i), we get</p>\n<p>5 = A[(–1)<sup>2</sup> + 9]</p>\n<p>∴ 5 = 10A</p>\n<p>∴ A = `1/2`</p>\n<p>Putting t = 0 in (i), we get</p>\n<p>5 = A(0 + 9) + (0 + C) (0 + 1)</p>\n<p>∴ 5 = 9A + C</p>\n<p>∴ 5 = `9(1/2) + \"C\"`</p>\n<p>∴ C = `1/2`</p>\n<p>Putting t = 1 in (i), we get</p>\n<p>5 = A(1<sup>2</sup> + 9) + (B + C)(1 + 1)</p>\n<p>∴ 5 = 10A + 2B + 2C</p>\n<p>∴ 5 = `10(1/2) + 2B + 2(1/2)`</p>\n<p>∴ – 1 = 2B</p>\n<p>∴ B = `-1/2`</p>\n<p>∴ `5/((t + 1)(t^2 + 9)) = (1/2)/(t + 1) + (1/2t + 1/2)/(t^2 + 9)`</p>\n<p>∴ I = `int((1/2)/(t+ 1) + ((-1)/2t + 1/2)/(t^2 + 9)) dt`</p>\n<p>= `1/2 [int 1/(t + 1) dt - int  t/(t^2 + 9) dt + int  1/(t^2 + 9) dt]`</p>\n<p>= `1/2[int 1/(t + 1) dt - 1/2  int (2t)/(t^2 + 9) dt + int 1/(t^2 + 3^2) dt]`</p>\n<p>= `1/2 [log (t + 1) - 1/2 log (t^2 + 9) + 1/3tan^-1(t/3)] + c`</p>\n<p>∴ I = `1/2  log (e^x + 1) - 1/4  log (e^(2x) + 9) + 1/6  tan^-1 ((e^x)/3) + c`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2024","paperDate":"2024-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2acf0c106d148607841","_marksId":"6941a2acf0c106d148607841","q":"<p>Evaluate: `int (2x^2 - 3)/((x^2 - 5)(x^2 + 4))dx`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Consider, `(2x^2 - 3)/((x^2 - 5)(x^2 + 4))`</p>\n<p>Let x<sup>2</sup> = m</p>\n<p>∴ `(2m - 3)/((m - 5)(m + 4))`  ...[proper rational function]</p>\n<p>Now, `(2m - 3)/((m - 5)(m + 4)) = A/((m - 5)) + B/((m + 4))`</p>\n<p>`(2m - 3)/((m - 5)(m + 4)) = (A(m + 4) + B(m - 5))/((m - 5)(m + 4))`</p>\n<p>∴ 2m – 3 = A (m + 4) + B (m – 5)</p>\n<p>at m = 5, 2(5) – 3 = A (9) + B (0)</p>\n<p>7 = 9A `\\implies` A = `7/9`</p>\n<p>at m = –4, 2(–4) – 3 = A (0) + B (–9)</p>\n<p>–11 = –9B `\\implies` B = `11/9`</p>\n<p>Thus, `(2m - 3)/((m - 5)(m + 4)) = ((7/9))/((m - 5)) + ((11/9))/((m + 4))` i.e. `(2x^2 - 3)/((x^2 - 5)(x^2 + 4)) = ((7/9))/((x^2 - 5)) + ((11/9))/((x^2 + 4))`</p>\n<p>∴ I = `int [((7/9))/(x^2 - 5) + ((11/9))/(x^2 + 4)]dx`</p>\n<p>= `7/9 . int 1/(x^2 - (sqrt(5))^2)dx + 11/9 . int 1/(x^2 + (2)^2)dx`</p>\n<p>= `7/9 . 1/(2(sqrt(5))) . log [(x - sqrt(5))/(x + sqrt(5))] + 11/9 . 1/2 . tan^-1 (x/2) + c`</p>\n<p>∴  I = `7/(18(sqrt(5))) . log [(x - sqrt(5))/(x + sqrt(5))] + 11/8 . tan^-1 (x/2) + c`</p>\n<p>∴ `int (2x^2 - 3)/((x^2 - 5)(x^2 + 4))dx = 7/(18(sqrt5)) . log [(x - sqrt(5))/(x + sqrt(5))] + 11/8 . tan^-1 (x/2) + c`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2023","paperDate":"2023-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d148607814","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d148607814","q":"<p><strong>If u and v ore differentiable functions of x. then prove that:</strong></p>\n<p>`int uv  dx = u intv  dx - int [(du)/(d) intv  dx]dx`</p>\n<p>Hence evaluate `intlog x  dx`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let `intv  dx`= w   ......(i)</p>\n<p>Then, `(dw)/(dx)` = v   ......(ii)</p>\n<p>Now, `d/(dx)(u, w) = u. d/(dx)(w) + w d/(dx)(u)`</p>\n<p>= `u.v + w  (du)/(dx)`  ......[From (ii)]</p>\n<p>By definition of integration</p>\n<p>u.w = `int[u.v + w . (du)/(dx)]dx`</p>\n<p>∴ u.w = `intu.v  dx + intw.  (du)/(dx) dx`</p>\n<p>∴ `intu.v  dx = u.w - intw.  (du)/(dx) dx`</p>\n<p>= `uintv  dx - int[(du)/(dx) intv.  dx]dx`  ......[Using (i)]</p>\n<p>Hence, `intlogx  dx = xlogx - int  1/x x xx dx`</p>\n<p>= x log x – x + C</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2022","paperDate":"2022-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077e7","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077e7","q":"<p> Prove that: `int \"dx\"/(sqrt(\"x\"^2 +\"a\"^2)) = log  |\"x\" +sqrt(\"x\"^2 +\"a\"^2) | + \"c\"`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let I = `int  1/sqrt(\"x\"^2 + \"a\"^2) \"dx\"`</p>\n<p>Put x = a tan θ ⇒ tan θ = `\"x\"/\"a\"`</p>\n<p>∴ dx = a sec<sup>2</sup> θ dθ </p>\n<p>∴ I = `int  1/ sqrt(\"a\"^2 \"tan\"^2 theta +\"a\"^2) \"a\"  \"sec\"^2  theta  \"d\" theta`</p>\n<p>= `int  (\"a\".\"sec\"^2 theta)/(\"a\" sqrt(1+\"tan\"^2 theta))     \"d\"theta`</p>\n<p>= `int  (\"sec\"^2 theta)/(\"sec\" theta) \"d\"theta `</p>\n<p>`= int  \"sec\" theta . \"d\" theta`</p>\n<p>`= \"log\"   |\"sec\" theta +\"tan\" theta| +\"c\"_1`</p>\n<p>`= \"log\" |\"x\"/\"a\" + sqrt(\"sec\"^2 theta)| + \"c\"_1`</p>\n<p>`= \"log\" | \"x\"/\"a\" + sqrt 1+ \"tan\"^2 theta | + \"c\"_1`</p>\n<p>=`\"log\" |\"x\" /\"a\" +sqrt(1+\"x\"^2/\"a\"^2)| +\"c\"_1`</p>\n<p>=` \"log\" |\"x\"/\"a\" + sqrt( \"a\"^2 + \"x\"^2)/\"a\"| + \"c\"_1`</p>\n<p>`= \"log\" |\"x\" +sqrt(\"x\"^2 +\"a\"^2)| - \"log\" \"a\" + \"c\"_1`</p>\n<p>`therefore int  1/sqrt(\"x\"^2 + \"a\"^2) \"dx\" = \"log\" |\"x\" +sqrt(\"x\"^2 +\"a\"^2)| - \"log\" \"a\" + \"c\" ,`</p>\n<p>where c = - log a +c<sub>1</sub></p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2019","paperDate":"2019-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d1486077bf","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d1486077bf","q":"<p><strong>Prove that:</strong></p>\n<p>`int 1/(a^2 - x^2) dx = 1/2 a log ((a +x)/(a-x)) + c`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Let I = `int1/(a^2 - x^2)dx`</p>\n<p>= `intdx/((a - x)(a + x))`</p>\n<p>= `1/(2a) int (1/(a + x) + 1/(a - x))dx`</p>\n<p>= `1/(2a) [int dx/(a + x) + int dx/(a - x)]`</p>\n<p>= `1/(2a) [log (a + x) + (log (a - x))/-1] + c`</p>\n<p>= `1/(2a) [log (a + x) - log (a - x)] + c`</p>\n<p>= `1/(2a) log ((a + x)/(a - x)) + c`</p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2018","paperDate":"2018-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"board_6941a2abf0c106d14860779c","_marksId":"6941a2abf0c106d14860779c","q":"<p>Find: `I=intdx/(sinx+sin2x)`</p>","options":[],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>`I=intdx/(sinx+sin2x)`</p>\n<p>`=int1/(sinx+2sinxcosx)dx`</p>\n<p>`=int1/(sinx(1+2cosx))dx`</p>\n<p>`=intsinx/(sin^2x(1+2cosx))dx`</p>\n<p>Let u=cosx</p>\n<p><span class=\"MathJax\" id=\"MathJax-Element-57-Frame\"><span class=\"math\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2501\"><span class=\"mrow\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2502\"><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2503\">⇒</span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2504\">d</span><span class=\"mi\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2505\">u</span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2506\">=</span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2507\">−</span><span class=\"mi\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2508\">sin</span><span class=\"mi\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2509\">x</span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2510\">d</span><span class=\"mi\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2511\">x</span></span></span></span><br/><br/>Also,<br/><br/></p>\n<p>`sin^2x=1−cos^2x=1−u^2`</p>\n<p>`∴ I = ∫−1/((1−u^2)(1+2u))du`</p>\n<p>`=int 1/((1+u)(1-u)(1+2u))du`</p>\n<p>Using partial fractions, we get</p>\n<p>`1/((1+u)(1-u)(1+2u))=A/(1+u)+B/(1-u)+C/(1+2u)`</p>\n<p>`=&gt;−1=A(1−u)(1+2u)+B(1+u)(1+2u)+C(1+u)(1−u)`</p>\n<p>`⇒−1=A(1+u−2u^2)+B(1+3u+2u^2)+C(1−u^2)`</p>\n<p>`⇒−1=(−2A+2B−C)u^2+(A+3B)u+(A+B+C)`</p>\n<p><br/>Equating the respective coefficients on the LHS and the RHS, we get</p>\n<p><span class=\"ya-q-full-text\"><span class=\"MathJax\" id=\"MathJax-Element-65-Frame\"><span class=\"math\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2791\"><span class=\"mrow\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2792\"><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2793\">−</span><span class=\"mn\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2794\">2</span><span class=\"mi\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2795\">A</span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2796\">+</span><span class=\"mn\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2797\">2</span><span class=\"mi\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2798\">B</span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2799\">−</span><span class=\"mi\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2800\">C</span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2801\">=</span><span class=\"mn\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2802\">0</span><span class=\"mspace\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2803\"></span></span></span></span>  .....(1)<br/><br/><span class=\"MathJax\" id=\"MathJax-Element-66-Frame\"><span class=\"math\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2804\"><span class=\"mrow\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2805\"><span class=\"mi\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2806\">A</span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2807\">+</span><span class=\"mn\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2808\">3</span><span class=\"mi\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2809\">B</span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2810\">=</span><span class=\"mn\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2811\">0</span></span></span></span>               .....(2)</span><br/><br/><span class=\"ya-q-full-text\"><span class=\"MathJax\" id=\"MathJax-Element-67-Frame\"><span class=\"math\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2812\"><span class=\"mrow\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2813\"><span class=\"mi\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2814\">A</span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2815\">+</span><span class=\"mi\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2816\">B</span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2817\">+</span><span class=\"mi\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2818\">C</span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2819\">=</span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2820\">−</span><span class=\"mn\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2821\">1</span></span></span></span>  .....(3)</span><br/><br/><span class=\"ya-q-full-text\">Adding (1), (2) and (3), we get<br/><br/><span class=\"MathJax\" id=\"MathJax-Element-68-Frame\"><span class=\"math\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2822\"><span class=\"mrow\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2823\"><span class=\"mn\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2824\">6</span><span class=\"mi\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2825\">B</span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2826\">=</span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2827\">−</span><span class=\"mn\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2828\">1</span></span></span></span><br/><br/><span class=\"MathJax\" id=\"MathJax-Element-69-Frame\"><span class=\"math\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2829\"><span class=\"mrow\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2830\"><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2831\">⇒</span><span class=\"mi\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2832\">B</span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2833\">=</span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2834\">−</span><span class=\"mfrac\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2835\"><span class=\"mn\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2836\">1/</span><span class=\"mn\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2837\">6</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2838\"></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"ya-q-full-text\"><span class=\"MathJax\"><span class=\"math\"><span class=\"mrow\"><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"mn\">From (2), we get<br/><br/><span class=\"MathJax\" id=\"MathJax-Element-70-Frame\"><span class=\"math\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2839\"><span class=\"mrow\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2840\"><span class=\"mi\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2841\">A</span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2842\">=</span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2843\">−</span><span class=\"mn\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2844\">3</span><span class=\"mi\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2845\">B</span></span></span></span><br/><br/><span class=\"MathJax\" id=\"MathJax-Element-71-Frame\"><span class=\"math\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2846\"><span class=\"mrow\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2847\"><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2848\">⇒</span><span class=\"mi\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2849\">A</span><span class=\"mo\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2850\">=</span><span class=\"mfrac\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2851\"><span class=\"mn\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2852\">1/</span><span class=\"mn\" id=\"MathJax-Span-2853\">2</span></span></span></span></span><br/><br/>From (3), we get<br/></span></span></span></span></span></span><br/><span id=\"MathJax-Element-72-Frame\"><span id=\"MathJax-Span-2854\"><span id=\"MathJax-Span-2855\"><span id=\"MathJax-Span-2856\">C</span><span id=\"MathJax-Span-2857\">=</span><span id=\"MathJax-Span-2858\">−</span><span id=\"MathJax-Span-2859\">1</span><span id=\"MathJax-Span-2860\">−</span><span id=\"MathJax-Span-2861\">A</span><span id=\"MathJax-Span-2862\">−</span><span id=\"MathJax-Span-2863\">B</span></span></span></span><br/><br/><span id=\"MathJax-Element-73-Frame\"><span id=\"MathJax-Span-2864\"><span id=\"MathJax-Span-2865\"><span id=\"MathJax-Span-2866\">⇒</span><span id=\"MathJax-Span-2867\">C</span><span id=\"MathJax-Span-2868\">=</span><span id=\"MathJax-Span-2869\">−</span><span id=\"MathJax-Span-2870\"><span id=\"MathJax-Span-2871\">4/</span><span id=\"MathJax-Span-2872\">3</span></span></span></span></span><br/><br/>So,<span class=\"ya-q-full-text\"><span class=\"MathJax\"><span class=\"math\"><span class=\"mrow\"><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"mn\"><br/></span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n<p>`1/((1+u)(1-u)(1+2u))=1/(2(1+u))-1/(6(1-u))-4/(3(1+2u))`</p>\n<p>`=&gt;I=int[1/(2(1+u))-1/(6(1-u))-4/(3(1+2u))]du`</p>\n<p>`= 1/2log(1+u)+1/6log(1−u)−4/(xx2)log(1+2u)+C`</p>\n<p>`= 1/2log(1+cosx)+1/6log(1−cosx)−2/3log(1+2cosx)+C` </p><br><br>","subject":"Mathematics & Statistics","chapter":"Indefinite Integration","exam":"HSC","examName":"HSC Board","_bank":"board","questionType":"subjective","source":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperSource":"HSC Boards - 2017","paperDate":"2017-03-01T09:00:00.000Z"}]}